with the private key for ID\emph{i} which \emph{B} then forwards to
\emph{A}. However, in the unlikely event that ID\emph{i} = ID\emph{∗},
algorithm \emph{B} cannot respond to this query. In this case, \emph{B}
terminates the simulation, picks a random bit \emph{b′}, and outputs
